# The source distribution carries the package, not the test suite.
#
# setuptools adds top-level tests/test*.py files on its own, but not
# tests/conftest.py or tests/_paths.py. Run from an unpacked sdist, those tests
# either failed to import or ran without the conftest that isolates them, and
# wrote to the user's real ~/.rag_knowledge. Many also read docs/, examples/
# and e2e/, which the sdist does not carry. Run the suite from a git checkout.
prune tests
